[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Puma at Large]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.68]Lesson 1 | 第1课
[00:02.36]A puma at large | 逃遁的美洲狮
[00:09.81]Where must the puma have come from? | 那只美洲狮究竟是从哪儿来的呢？
[00:14.48]Pumas are large, cat-like animals which are found in America. | 美洲狮是体形似猫的大型动物，产于美洲。
[00:19.17]When reports came into London Zoo that a wild puma had been spotted forty-five miles south of London, | 当伦敦动物园接到报告说，在伦敦以南45英里处发现一只野生美洲狮时，
[00:26.27]they were not taken seriously. | 这些报告并没有受到重视。
[00:29.15]However, as the evidence began to accumulate, | 然而，随着证据越积越多，
[00:33.21]experts from the Zoo felt obliged to investigate, | 动物园的专家们感到有必要进行一番调查，
[00:37.15]for the descriptions given by people who claimed to have seen the puma were extraordinarily similar. | 因为凡是声称见过这只美洲狮的人所描述的样子出奇地相似。
[00:43.86]The hunt for the puma began in a small village where a woman picking blackberries saw 'a large cat'only five yards away from her. | 搜寻美洲狮的工作是从一个小村庄开始的，那里的一位采黑莓的妇女看见“一只大猫”，离她仅5码远。
[00:53.61]It immediately ran away when she saw it, | 她刚看见它，它就立刻跑开了，
[00:56.49]and experts confirmed that a puma will not attack a human being unless it is cornered. | 专家们证实说，美洲狮除非被逼得走投无路，是不会伤人的。
[01:02.94]The search proved difficult, | 搜寻工作证实很困难，
[01:05.20]for the puma was often observed at one place in the morning and at another place twenty miles away in the evening. | 因为常常是早晨在甲地见到那只美洲狮，晚上却在20英里外的乙地发现它的踪影。
[01:12.58]Wherever it went, it left behind it a trail of dead deer and small animals like rabbits. | 无论它走到哪儿，身后总会留下死鹿和兔子之类的小动物的一串踪迹。
[01:19.38]Paw prints were seen in a number of places and puma fur was found clinging to bushes. | 许多地方看见了爪印，灌木丛上还发现了粘着的美洲狮毛。
[01:25.39]Several people complained of 'cat-like noises' at night and a businessman on a fishing trip saw the puma up a tree. | 有人抱怨夜里听见“像猫一样的叫声”；一位外出钓鱼的商人看见那只美洲狮爬在树上。
[01:34.26]The experts were now fully convinced that the animal was a puma, | 专家们此刻已完全肯定那只动物就是美洲狮，
[01:38.72]but where had it come from? | 但它是从哪儿来的呢？
[01:41.27]As no pumas had been reported missing from any zoo in the country, | 由于全国没有一家动物园报告丢了美洲狮，
[01:45.55]this one must have been in the possession of a private collector and somehow managed to escape. | 这只美洲狮肯定是某位私人收藏家豢养的，不知怎么设法逃了出来。
[01:52.16]The hunt went on for several weeks, | 搜寻工作持续了好几个星期，
[01:54.18]but the puma was not caught. | 但始终未能逮住那只美洲狮。
[01:57.42]It is disturbing to think that a dangerous wild animal is still at large in the quiet countryside. | 想到在宁静的乡村还有一只危险的野兽在逍遥法外，真令人担忧。
